# Sprint 5 — Attendance (Grade-Based)

## Overview

Sprint 5 builds attendance, but not as a single mechanism for everyone. Facial recognition applies only to secondary students (grades 8–12). Primary students (grades 1–7) get a traditional manual roll-call register instead — deliberately avoiding a biometric, workplace-style check-in for young children, while giving secondary students something closer to a professional check-in environment as preparation for the world beyond school.

## Goals

- Add a `grade` field to `User` so attendance can route by grade band
- Build a manual roll-call register for primary students (1–7)
- Build facial-recognition check-in/check-out for secondary students (8–12), with consent and a manual fallback
- Land both mechanisms on one shared `Attendance` model, so later sprints don't need to know which method produced a record
- Enforce grade-based routing at the view level, not just in the UI

## What was built

- **`User.grade`** — integer field, 1–12, added to the existing student registration form from Sprint 1 as a required field for students. A small addition to existing auth, not new auth work.
- **`Attendance` model** — student (FK), date, `method` (`"manual"` / `"facial"`), `arrived_at` (nullable), `departed_at` (nullable). One record per student per day, enforced at the database level. Viewable and markable by any teacher — not scoped to whoever created the record, since this is a shared front-desk function, not personal marking work.
- **Primary flow (grades 1–7)** — a register view listing all grade 1–7 students (no class/roster structure yet, same known limitation as Sprints 3/4). Teacher ticks who's present, submits; creates `Attendance(method="manual", arrived_at=now)` per student for today. No `departed_at` tracking — a register records presence, not clock-in/clock-out. A student with no record for the day is implicitly absent.
- **`FaceEnrollment` model (secondary only)** — student (FK), stored face descriptor (never the source photo), enrolled-by, enrolled-at, and a `consent_confirmed` boolean the enrolling teacher must explicitly check
- **Enrollment flow** — teacher selects a secondary student, captures a reference photo via browser camera, confirms consent, saves. Re-enrolling updates the existing descriptor rather than duplicating it.
- **Check-in/check-out flow (secondary)** — camera captures a frame, face-api.js matches against enrolled descriptors. On match: sets `arrived_at` if unset today, otherwise `departed_at`, `method="facial"`.
- **Shared manual fallback** — a failed facial match reuses the exact same manual-marking mechanism the primary flow uses, rather than a second, duplicated manual-entry path
- **Grade-based routing enforced server-side** — a grade 1–7 student is never offered facial enrollment; a grade 8–12 student doesn't appear in the manual roll-call list except via the fallback path. Enforced at the view level based on `User.grade`, not hidden UI.
- **Attendance history** — a list viewable by any teacher, showing who's been marked present today across both methods, with the method that produced each record

## Definition of done

- [x] `User.grade` added and required at student registration
- [x] Manual roll-call for primary students creates correct one-per-student-per-day records
- [x] Secondary student enrollment requires explicit consent and stores only the descriptor, never the photo
- [x] Secondary check-in/check-out works via face match
- [x] A failed facial match falls back to the shared manual-marking mechanism — no duplicated logic
- [x] Grade-based routing is enforced at the view level in both directions
- [x] One attendance record per student per day enforced at the database level
- [x] Attendance is viewable/markable by any teacher, not scoped to one teacher's records
- [x] All views reject non-teacher roles, consistent with existing sprints
- [x] Tests cover the grade addition, manual roll-call, consent-gatedenrollment, successful and failed facial match, the shared fallback, routing enforcement for both grade bands, and multi-teacher access
- [x] New test module added to the sprint-to-module mapping in `run.sh` so `./run.sh sprint 5` and `./run.sh sprint-pg 5` pick it up

## Out of scope for this sprint

Student or parent-facing attendance views (Sprint 6/7), continuous or live facial detection (already rejected earlier), attendance reporting or analytics.

## Known limitations

- **No class/roster structure yet** (carried over from Sprints 3/4) — the primary roll-call lists every grade 1–7 student, not a specific teacher's class.
- **Absence is implicit, not explicit.** A student with no attendance record for the day is treated as absent by omission; there's no explicit "marked absent" state yet.
- **Parent-student linking is still self-declared and unverified**
  (carried over from Sprint 1) — unchanged by this sprint.

